  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Hosea",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 12,
    "summary": "The Lord uses prophets, visions, and similitudes to guide His people, but they become rich and will not wait on the Lord—Ephraim provokes Him most bitterly.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Ephraim feedeth on wind, and followeth after the east wind: he daily increaseth lies and desolation; and they do make a covenant with the Assyrians, and oil is carried into Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Isa. 28:1 (1–8)."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "Hosea 5:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord hath also a controversy with Judah, and will punish Jacob according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "Hosea 4:1 (1–2)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He took his brother by the heel in the womb, and by his strength he had power with God:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Gen. 25:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, he had power over the angel, and prevailed: he wept, and made supplication unto him: he found him in Beth-el, and there he spake with us;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Angels."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Gen. 32:28 (24–28)."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 113,
            "text": "Gen. 28:13 (10–16)."
          },
          {
            "start": 139,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "OR him."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even the Lord God of hosts; the Lord is his memorial.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "Ex. 3:15 (13–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore turn thou to thy God: keep mercy and judgment, and wait on thy God continually.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Conversion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He is a merchant, the balances of deceit are in his hand: he loveth to oppress.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Micah 6:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ephraim said, Yet I am become rich, I have found me out substance: in all my labours they shall find none iniquity in me that were sin.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          },
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 134
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I that am the Lord thy God from the land of Egypt will yet make thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in the days of the solemn feast.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "OR tents. Lev. 23:34."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have also spoken by the prophets, and I have multiplied visions, and used similitudes, by the ministry of the prophets.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Is there iniquity in Gilead? surely they are vanity: they sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yea, their altars are as heaps in the furrows of the fields.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Hosea 9:15 (13–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 109
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jacob fled into the country of Syria, and Israel served for a wife, and for a wife he kept sheep.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Gen. 28:5; Deut. 26:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "Gen. 29:20 (15–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And by a prophet the Lord brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet was he preserved.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:24 (24–26)."
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Ex. 12:50."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ephraim provoked him to anger most bitterly: therefore shall he leave his blood upon him, and his reproach shall his Lord return unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "IE guilt."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
